„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter+¨sections–…¤book§chapter+«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­But now thus saith the LORD that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O Israel, Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙØWhen thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxFor I am the LORD thy God, the Holy One of Israel, thy Saviour: I gave Egypt for thy ransom, Ethiopia and Seba for thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”Since thou wast precious in my sight, thou hast been honourable, and I have loved thee: therefore will I give men for thee, and people for thy life.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaFear not: for I am with thee: I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡I will say to the north, Give up; and to the south, Keep not back: bring my sons from far, and my daughters from the ends of the earth;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙweven every one that is called by my name: for I have created him for my glory, I have formed him; yea, I have made him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter+«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIBring forth the blind people that have eyes, and the deaf that have ears.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙğLet all the nations be gathered together, and let the people be assembled: who among them can declare this, and shew us former things? let them bring forth their witnesses, that they may be justified: or let them hear, and say, It is truth.¦layout ªlast_ver