¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÉYe are my witnesses, saith the LORD, and my servant whom I have chosen: that ye may know and believe me, and understand that I am he: before me there was no God formed, neither shall there be after me.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:I, even I, am the LORD; and beside me there is no saviour.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšI have declared, and have saved, and I have shewed, when there was no strange god among you: therefore ye are my witnesses, saith the LORD, that I am God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvYea, before the day was I am he; and there is none that can deliver out of my hand: I will work, and who shall let it?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter+«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ·Thus saith the LORD, your redeemer, the Holy One of Israel; For your sake I have sent to Babylon, and have brought down all their nobles, and the Chaldeans, whose cry is in the ships.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ?I am the LORD, your Holy One, the creator of Israel, your King.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter+«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTThus saith the LORD, which maketh a way in the sea, and a path in the mighty waters;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢which bringeth forth the chariot and horse, the army and the power; they shall lie down together, they shall not rise: they are extinct, they are quenched as tow.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFRemember ye not the former things, neither consider the things of old.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«The beast of the field shall honour me, the dragons and the owls: because I give waters in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert, to give drink to my people, my chosen.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFThis people have I formed for myself; they shall shew forth my praise.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter+«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTBut thou hast not called upon me, O Jacob; but thou hast been weary of me, O Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÅThou hast not brought me the small cattle of thy burnt offerings; neither hast thou honoured me with thy sacrifices. I have not caused thee to serve with an offering, nor wearied thee with incense.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃThou hast bought me no sweet cane with money, neither hast thou filled me with the fat of thy sacrifices: but thou hast made me to serve with thy sins, thou hast wearied me with thine iniquities.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter+«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhI, even I, am he that blotteth out thy transgressions for mine own sake, and will not remember thy sins.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZPut me in remembrance: let us plead together: declare thou, that thou mayest be justified.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLThy first father hath sinned, and thy teachers have transgressed against me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtTherefore I have profaned the princes of the sanctuary, and have given Jacob to the curse, and Israel to reproaches.¦layout ªlast_verse